+# P1 — Gen 2 onboarding decoupling
+
+**Status:** Implemented in this repo. Public WP `/onboarding/` is **not** redirected yet.  
+**Rule:** WordPress is not a DigitalGate onboarding fallback or source of truth.
+
+## Journey (single definition)
+
+`GEN2_ONBOARDING_STEPS` in `packages/platform-core/src/onboarding/gen2-journey.ts`:
+
+Welcome → Identity → Business Profile → Goals → **Team** → **Systems** → Plan → Apps → Cadence → Order → Stripe → Connect → Checklist → Implementation
+
+`/founding/setup` is a gate (agreement) then the **same** `/onboarding` wizard.
+
+## Sources of truth (Neon)
+
+| Step | Stored on |
+|------|-----------|
+| Business Profile | `organisation.settings.profile` |
+| Goals | Organisation goals + `gen2Onboarding.goalIds` |
+| Team | `Membership` (+ pending `invite:` seats) |
+| Systems | `organisation.settings.systems` + connector blobs for known ids |
+| Plan / Apps | `gen2Onboarding.platformTier` / `industryApps` / `premiumApps` |
+| Resume cursor | `organisation.settings.gen2Onboarding` |
+
+## Retired from the request path
+
+- `fetchPortalMe` → WordPress `GET /portal/me`
+- `pingApi` → WordPress `OPTIONS /onboarding`
+- `ensureOrganisationOnboardingSync` / `syncOrganisationFromPortal` on page load
+- `POST /api/webhooks/dg-onboarding-sync` applying portal entitlements
+- UI links to `https://digitalgate.com.au/onboarding/`
+
+## DECOUPLED test
+
+```bash
+# Block WP
+unset DG_API_BASE_URL DG_WP_CONNECTOR_BASE_URL DG_ONBOARDING_URL
+# Optional: stop WordPress entirely
+
+npm run test:p1-onboarding
+```
+
+Then, signed into Gen 2 with Neon + Clerk (WP process down):
+
+1. Open `/onboarding`
+2. Complete Business Profile, Goals, Team, Systems, Plan, Apps
+3. Leave mid-wizard, reopen `/onboarding` — resume on `currentStep`
+4. Confirm Network: zero `/wp-json/digitalgate/v1/portal/me` or WP `/onboarding`
+5. `/founding/setup` (after agreement) lands on the same wizard
+6. `/signup` is unchanged
+
+Do not 301 the public WP `/onboarding/` URL until this path is signed off in production.
